  "vulnerability_information": "## Summary\n\nOn Windows with SSPI/Negotiate, curl 8.21.0 can reuse a connection authenticated with ambient credentials for a later request using different explicit credentials.\n\nIn `url_match_auth_nego()`, the credential comparison is skipped when `conn->creds == NULL`. This allows a connection authenticated as one identity to be reused for a request configured with another identity. In my reproducer, request A authenticates as `Administrator`, request B supplies credentials for `userB`, but the server processes B as `Administrator`.\n\ncurl 8.20.0 does not reproduce this issue.\n\n## Affected version\n\nReproduced with libcurl 8.21.0 on Windows using SSPI/SPNEGO.\n\n## Root cause\n\nIn 8.21.0:\n\n```c\nif(m->want_nego_http) {\n  if(conn->creds &&\n     (!Curl_creds_same(conn->creds, m->data->state.creds) ||\n      !Curl_peer_equal(conn->creds_origin, m->data->state.origin)))\n    return FALSE;\n}\n```\n\nThe credential/origin comparison is only performed when `conn->creds` is non-NULL. Connections authenticated through ambient SSPI credentials can have `conn->creds == NULL`, so the check is skipped.\n\n## Steps To Reproduce\n\n1. Run the attached local Windows Negotiate server.\n2. Run the PoC as Windows user A (`Administrator` in my test).\n3. Request A uses `CURLAUTH_NEGOTIATE` without explicit credentials.\n4. Request B uses another easy handle on the same `CURLM` with explicit credentials for `userB`.\n5. On curl 8.21.0, request B reuses A's connection.\n\nObserved:\n\n```text\n8.20.0:\nA default        -> Administrator\nB explicit userB -> userB\n\n8.21.0:\nA default        -> Administrator\nB explicit userB -> Administrator\n```\n\nDisabling connection reuse causes B to authenticate correctly as `userB`.\n\nAttached:\n\n* `poc.c` - minimal libcurl reproducer\n* `server.cs` - minimal local Negotiate server\n\n## Impact\n\nA request configured for one user may execute using the identity of a previously authenticated pooled connection.\n\n## Suggested fix\n\nThe credential/origin comparison should depend on whether the connection has entered Negotiate authentication state, rather than whether `conn->creds` is non-NULL:\n\n```diff\n if(m->want_nego_http) {\n-  if(conn->creds &&\n+  if((conn->http_negotiate_state != GSS_AUTHNONE) &&\n      (!Curl_creds_same(conn->creds, m->data->state.creds) ||\n       !Curl_peer_equal(conn->creds_origin, m->data->state.origin)))\n     return FALSE;\n }\n```\n",
